4908":"tabernacle","H1980":"went","H1696":"speak","H854":"with","H259":"one","H8199":"to judge","H6680":"to command","H7462":"House of Shepherds","H5971":"people","H4100":"what?","H6258":"now","H6635":"army","H589":"I","H3947":"take","H5116":"pasture","H310":"after","H6629":"flock","H5057":"leader","H5921":"upon","H3772":"cut","H341":"enemy","H6440":"before","H8034":"name","H1419":"large","H776":"country/planet","H7760":"make","H4725":"place","H5193":"to plant","H7931":"to dwell","H7264":"to tremble","H5750":"still","H3254":"again","H1121":"child","H5766":"injustice","H1086":"to become old","H7223":"first","H3665":"be humble","H5046":"to tell","H4390":"to fill","H1":"father","H6965":"(Leb)-kamai","H2233":"seed","H3559":"prepare","H4438":"royalty","H3678":"throne","H5769":"enduring","H2617":"kindness","H5493":"remove","H5975":"stand","H428":"these","H2377":"vision","H3651":"right","H935":"come","H4428":"king","H4310":"who?","H1988":"here","H6994":"be small","H2063":"this","H5869":"eye","H7350":"distant","H7200":"see","H8448":"border","H120":"man","H4609":"thought","H3519":"glory","H3045":"to know","H5668":"for the sake of","H3820":"heart","H1420":"greatness","H369":"nothing","H3644":"like","H2108":"exception","H8085":"hear","H241":"ear","H1471":"nation","H6299":"to ransom","H3372":"to fear","H1644":"drive out","H4714":"Egypt","H5414":"give","H539":"be faithful","H1431":"to magnify","H1540":"Heglam","H4672":"to find","H6419":"to pray","H2896":"pleasant","H2974":"be willing","H1288":"to bless"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Cedar. Such were esteemed the most magnificent, ver. 6. See 2 Kings vii."],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","A place permanent and secure, while I have had no fixed abode. (Calmet) — No more, for a long time: and unless they provoke me by their crimes, as they did afterwards, and were exposed to more severe chastisements. Constant rest is not always expedient. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Seed, even till Christ shall be born of the Blessed Virgin, of the family of David."],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Ever often means only a long duration. The dominion of Christ shall have no end. (Calmet) — The Church founded by this true David, (Haydock) falls heir to these promises. (Du Hamel)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Thee. The posterity of Saul lost the throne. (Haydock) — If Solomon was reprobated, his children were permitted to reign. It is also presumed that he did penance; though this is not certain."],["haydock",17,null,"haydock","Men. Who was ever more favoured by God than David? Hebrew, “Thou hast regarded me according to the estate of a man of high degree.” (Protestants) (Haydock)"],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Known him. Treating him with love and tenderness, as a friend. How can David sufficiently testify his gratitude?"],["haydock",21,null,"haydock","Himself. Hebrew adds, “and to make thee a name.”"],["haydock",27,null,"haydock","Begun. Hebrew, “be pleased, (Haydock) or thou hast had the goodness to bless.” Syriac, “I pray thee bless."]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]},"fa":[[11,13,0,"The Proof of the Gospel","Book 7",0,339,"… \"He shall be great, and shall be called the Son of the Highest, and the Lord God shall give to him the throne of his father David, and he shall rule over the house of Jacob for ever; and of his kingdom there shall be no end.\" And after a little, Zacharias the father of John, prophesies thus concerning Christ in the same gospel: \"Blessed be the Lord God of Israel, for he hath visited and wrought redemption for his people, and hath raised a horn of salvation for us in the house of David his son, as he spake by the mouth of his holy prophets from ages past.\" …"]],"fau":[["eusebius","Eusebius of Caesarea",0,"ecclesiastical-writer",null,1,339]],"ftr":[["W. J. Ferrar, The Proof of the Gospel (SPCK, 1920)"]]}